-- title:
--   Invertible ideal sheaf: I ⊗ I^∨ ≅ mathcal O_X, both orders
-- statement:
--   Let $X$ be a scheme and let $I$ be a quasi-coherent ideal sheaf datum on $X$, assumed invertible in the sense of the predicate `IsInvertible`: for every point $x$ of $X$ there are an affine open $U$ of $X$ and a section $f \in \Gamma(X,U)$ with $x$ in the basic open $X.\mathrm{basicOpen}\,f$, together with a non-zero-divisor $g \in \Gamma(X, X.\mathrm{affineBasicOpen}\,f)$ such that the ideal attached to $I$ on $X.\mathrm{affineBasicOpen}\,f$ is the principal ideal generated by $g$. Here `I.module` is the $\mathcal O_X$-module given as the kernel of the canonical map from the unit module $\mathcal O_X$ to the pushforward along the closed immersion $I.\mathrm{subschemeι}$ of the unit module of the associated closed subscheme, and `I.invModule` is its dual $\underline{\mathrm{Hom}}(I.\mathrm{module}, \mathbf 1)$ in the monoidal category $X.\mathrm{Modules}$. The conclusion asserts that both of the types of isomorphisms $I.\mathrm{module} \otimes I.\mathrm{invModule} \cong \mathbf 1$ and $I.\mathrm{invModule} \otimes I.\mathrm{module} \cong \mathbf 1$ in $X.\mathrm{Modules}$ are non-empty, the unit $\mathbf 1$ being the structure sheaf as a module over itself. Existence of the isomorphisms is asserted, with no compatibility or canonicity claimed.
--
--   This is the statement that for an effective Cartier divisor $Z$ on $X$, with $\mathcal O_X(-Z) = \mathcal I$ and $\mathcal O_X(Z) = \mathcal{H}om(\mathcal I, \mathcal O_X)$, one has $\mathcal O_X(-Z) \otimes \mathcal O_X(Z) \cong \mathcal O_X$ in either order, i.e. that the class of $\mathcal O_X(-Z)$ is invertible in the Picard group. It is used throughout the treatment of relative effective Cartier divisors, line bundles on curves and the relative Picard functor, for instance in identifying pullbacks of ideal-sheaf modules with line bundles attached to points.
